.IX Title "ISCSI_SCST_ADM 8"
.TH ISCSI_SCST_ADM 8 "2007-05" "iSCSI SCST Target admin" "User Manuals"
.SH "NAME"
iscsi-scst-adm \- legacy iSCSI-SCST runtime administration utility
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBiscsi-scst-adm [OPTION]\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
iscsi-scst-adm is a legacy client for monitoring and modifying the runtime
state held by iscsi-scstd. The daemon accepts requests only from clients whose
user and group IDs are both zero.
.PP
The utility does not update /etc/iscsi-scstd.conf, so runtime changes can be
lost when iscsi-scstd is restarted. Use scstadmin and /etc/scst.conf for new
configurations.
.PP
Account operations place CHAP passwords in process arguments. Take care not to
expose them through local process inspection or command history.
.SH "USAGE"
.IX Header "USAGE"
The utility addresses targets and sessions by numeric ID. Target IDs are
available under /sys/kernel/scst_tgt/targets/iscsi/*/tid and active session
IDs under /sys/kernel/scst_tgt/targets/iscsi/*/sessions/*/sid.
.PP
For example:
.PP
\&\fBiscsi-scst-adm \-\-op show \-\-tid=1\fR
.PP
display the parameters of target 1.
.PP
\&\fBiscsi-scst-adm \-\-op new \-\-tid=2 \-\-params Name=iqn.2007-05.com.example:target\fR
.PP
create runtime target 2 with the specified name. Add it to the persistent
configuration separately if it must survive a daemon restart.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.IX Header "OPTIONS"
\&\fB\-\-op new \-\-tid=[id] \-\-params Name=[name]\fR
.PP
add a new target with [id]. If [id] is zero, the lowest free [id] is
allocated automatically to the new target.
.PP
\&\fB\-\-op delete \-\-tid=[id]\fR
.PP
delete specific target with [id]. The target must
have no active sessions.
.PP
\&\fB\-\-op show \-\-tid=[id]\fR
.PP
show target parameters of target with [id].
.PP
\&\fB\-\-op show \-\-tid=[id] \-\-sid=[sid]\fR
.PP
show iSCSI parameters in effect for session [sid]. If
[sid] is \*(L"0\*(R" (zero), the configured parameters
will be displayed.
.PP
\&\fB\-\-op delete \-\-tid=[id] \-\-sid=[sid] \-\-cid=[cid]\fR
.PP
delete specific connection with [cid] in a session
with [sid] that the target with [id] has.
If the session has no connections after
the operation, the session will be deleted
automatically.
.PP
\&\fB\-\-op update \-\-tid=[id] \-\-params=key1=value1,key2=value2,...\fR
.PP
change iSCSI-SCST parameters for target [id]. Parameter names from
iscsi-scstd.conf can be used as keys.
.PP
\&\fB\-\-op new \-\-tid=[id] \-\-user \-\-params=[user]=[name],Password=[pass]\fR
.PP
add a new account with [pass] for specific target.
[user] could be [IncomingUser] or [OutgoingUser].
If you don't specify a target (omit \-\-tid option),
you add a new account for discovery sessions.
.PP
\&\fB\-\-op show \-\-tid=[id] \-\-user\fR
.PP
show a list of CHAP accounts.
If \-\-tid is omitted or [id] is \*(L"0\*(R" (zero), discovery accounts
are displayed.
.PP
\&\fB\-\-op show \-\-tid=[id] \-\-user \-\-params=[user]=[name]\fR
.PP
show CHAP account information for the account specified by [name].
[user] can be [IncomingUser] or [OutgoingUser].
If \-\-tid is omitted or [id] is \*(L"0\*(R" (zero), [name] is treated as
a discovery account name.
.PP
\&\fB\-\-op delete \-\-tid=[id] \-\-user \-\-params=[user]=[name]\fR
.PP
delete specific account having [name] of specific
target. [user] could be [IncomingUser] or
[OutgoingUser].
If you don't specify a target (omit \-\-tid option),
you delete the account for discovery sessions.
.PP
\&\fB\-\-version\fR
.PP
display version and exit
.PP
\&\fB\-\-help\fR
.PP
display a list of available options and exit
.SH "LIMITATIONS"
.IX Header "LIMITATIONS"
iscsi-scst-adm accepts numeric target IDs, not target names or aliases, and
does not read or modify /etc/iscsi-scstd.conf.
.SH "REPORTING BUGS"
.IX Header "REPORTING BUGS"
Report bugs to <scst\-devel@lists.sourceforge.net>.
.SH "FILES"
.IX Header "FILES"
/sys/kernel/scst_tgt/targets/iscsi/*/tid
.PP
/sys/kernel/scst_tgt/targets/iscsi/*/sessions/*/sid
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fIiscsi-scstd\fR\|(8),\fIiscsi-scstd.conf\fR\|(5)
